@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-timestamps-come-from-a-clock-injected-into-the-list
+type: decision-log
+title: "Timestamps come from a clock injected into the list"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+Tasks must record `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. `src/domain/` may not read the clock (r3).
+
+## Decision
+The domain takes a `now: () => string` (ISO-8601) and stamps tasks with it. `createTodoList` in
+`src/index.ts`, outside the domain, defaults it to the wall clock; tests pass a fixed or stepping clock.
+`updatedAt` changes only when a task really changes: completing, reopening, renaming to a different
+title, adding a tag it lacks, removing a tag it has. A failed or no-op call leaves it alone.
+
+## Consequences
+Timestamps are testable and deterministic. `createTask` and the task functions take the time as a
+parameter. Callers of `createTodoList()` need no change.
